local_dev_fixtures/

# Personal data (individuals' names, mailboxes, a direct phone number) split
# out of tools/anonymization_mapping.py. Never tracked; see that module's
# _resolve() for how it is spliced back in, and note it is NOT recoverable
# from git if lost.
tools/anonymization_pii_rules_local.py

# local
.DS_Store
venv/
.env*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# review_app_react/frontend build artifacts -- rebuilt via `npm run build`
# before any Databricks App deploy (see review_app_react/app.yaml)
review_app_react/frontend/node_modules/
# review_app_react/frontend/dist/ is TRACKED as of 2026-08-27 — see the note
# in review_app_react/frontend/.gitignore. The Databricks workspace folder is a
# Git folder with no build step, and the backend serves this directory.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-22: the anonymized demo pair (demo_frd.docx / demo_sttm.xlsx), the
# local_dev_fixtures/ inputs, and the tracked replay set
# (sttm_out_live_e2e_20260807b/) were REMOVED from the repo and from git's
# index -- no FRD/STTM material of any kind is tracked any more (they remain
# in history until a purge is decided). The `!` re-include negations that
# used to carve those files past the rules above were deleted with them on
# purpose: do NOT add them back. New fixture material must go through
# tools/ anonymization AND a deliberate decision before it is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local venv + editable-install build metadata
.venv/
src/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# LibreOffice/Excel lock files. `open`ing a tracked-directory .xlsx leaves one
# behind and it makes an otherwise-clean tree look dirty, which the workspace
# deploy script (scripts/deploy_to_workspace.sh) then refuses to push on.
.~lock.*#
~$*

# Databricks CLI state dropped wherever it is run from (2026-08-27: appeared in
# review_app_react/frontend/ after running the CLI there). Never repo content.
.databricks/
